    "created_at": "2016-04-25T20:08:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-25T20:08:00Z",
    "body": "> No, exceptions are handled by \"If evaluation was unsuccessful, let result be undefined instead.\"\n\nAh, in terms of the navigation behavior.  OK, good, I think that matches all UAs.  What about the onerror/reporting behavior?\n\nIn Gecko, we basically report the exception then pretend like execution succeeded and returned undefined.\n",
