    "created_at": "2016-04-27T00:32:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-27T00:32:05Z",
    "body": "Just curious, not objecting anything here, but do we know why non-Gecko engines don't do the obvious thing and convert the return value effectively to string? Like did anyone try to first file implementation bugs before this spec bug?\n(This change will break my calculator, which is to write javascript: 1+1, after this change I'll need to write javascript: 1+1+\"\")\n",
